values ('ap_statistics', 2, '2.11', array['2.11']::text[], 'convention', 'Interval notation for normal areas (p is a percentage)', 'P(X<x_a)=p/100 means the lowest p% lie left of x_a, P(x_a<X<x_b)=p/100 means p% lie between, P(X>x_b)=p/100 means the highest p% lie right of x_b, and the most extreme p% on both sides splits into p/200 in each tail.', '[]'::jsonb, NULL, 'Here p is a number between 0 and 100 (a percentage), not a proportion; boundaries can be found with technology or with z-scores and a standard normal table.', 'published', 'generated-checked; extractor=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; batch=ap-statistics-reference-u2-u3-2026-10-10; candidate=ap_statistics-u2-r1-037; ced=2.11.E.2.i-iv "p is defined as a number between 0 and 100"')
